; What a `parallel` binding may answer is a WORD, and the checker says
; so at the binding's expression.
;
; The thunk `parallel` builds for a binding is `(-> Int Int)` - codegen's
; `emitPrimPar` header records why: under processes the answer crosses
; an address space through one shared page, and under threads it would
; have to be promoted out of another arena, which is S3/S4's typed
; promotion and not this slice's. So a `String` here is `AX3004:
; expected Int, found String`, anchored on the literal and not on the
; word `parallel`; the second binding is a word and draws nothing.
(import IO)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (parallel p ((s "x") (n 2))
    n))
